1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,184
A careful point.

2
00:00:01,184 --> 00:00:08,515
Permanganate is intensely purple, but manganese seven is d zero, with no d electrons at all.

3
00:00:08,515 --> 00:00:15,312
Its colour comes from charge transfer: light moves an electron from an oxygen lone pair onto the metal.

4
00:00:15,312 --> 00:00:17,317
The same goes for dichromate.

5
00:00:17,317 --> 00:00:20,208
That is why these colours are so much more intense.

